WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.260 --> 00:00:02.185
Hi, welcome back to the Lam Rim.

00:00:02.185 --> 00:00:06.185
And as you can see, we are
starting with the peach tree.

00:00:06.185 --> 00:00:08.160
That is the real peach
tree outside of my house.

00:00:08.160 --> 00:00:11.298
We planted it this year,

00:00:11.298 --> 00:00:15.492
and somehow it grew very
well during the virus time.

00:00:17.392 --> 00:00:20.458
We were talking about a famous metaphor

00:00:20.458 --> 00:00:24.333
that was written about by Chandrakirti.

00:00:24.333 --> 00:00:26.383
He said:

00:00:26.383 --> 00:00:30.716
"Love is like the seed for the peach tree.

00:00:30.716 --> 00:00:35.716
Love is like the water &amp; the
fertilizer for the peach tree.

00:00:35.777 --> 00:00:39.876
Love is like eating the peach."

00:00:39.876 --> 00:00:42.202
THOG MTHA' BAR Tim,

00:00:42.202 --> 00:00:44.334
THOG MTHA' BAR

00:00:44.334 --> 00:00:49.084
In the beginning, in
the end, and in between.

00:00:49.084 --> 00:00:53.632
As a seed, as a fruit, and as a tree.

00:00:53.632 --> 00:00:56.944
Love is important in all three times.

00:00:56.944 --> 00:00:59.785
Then Tsongkhapa was careful to say,

00:00:59.785 --> 00:01:04.410
"Look, we are using three
different images of the tree,

00:01:04.410 --> 00:01:05.943
of the growth of the tree.

00:01:05.943 --> 00:01:08.001
But do not forget we are
talking about one love,

00:01:08.001 --> 00:01:09.548
the love is the same.

00:01:09.548 --> 00:01:13.631
The examples are three.
The examples are three:

00:01:13.631 --> 00:01:15.670
the seed of the tree,

00:01:15.670 --> 00:01:19.300
the growing of the tree, and
then the fruit of the tree.

00:01:19.300 --> 00:01:20.717
But really, we are just talking

00:01:20.717 --> 00:01:22.530
about one love, one single love.

00:01:22.530 --> 00:01:27.530
And that is why Chandrakirti
repeats the word love,

00:01:28.070 --> 00:01:31.530
love and only love.
Because he wants us to know

00:01:31.530 --> 00:01:35.270
that love is the example
in all three metaphors.

00:01:35.270 --> 00:01:37.200
All right, so, we are going to the

00:01:37.200 --> 00:01:39.549
back to the text of the Lam Rim.

00:01:39.549 --> 00:01:40.824
,ZHES GSUNGS PA BZHIN,

00:01:40.824 --> 00:01:43.223
THOG MAR THEG CHEN DU
NGES PAR BYED PA DANG,

00:01:43.223 --> 00:01:45.839
BYANG CHUB TU SEMS BSKYED
PA'I RTZA BAR GYUR PAS

00:01:45.839 --> 00:01:47.917
SA BON LTAR GAL CHE BA,

00:01:47.917 --> 00:01:52.917
SA BON LTAR means look, compassion.

00:01:53.624 --> 00:01:56.756
SNYING RJE -- karuna -- is like the seed.

00:01:56.756 --> 00:02:00.923
Why? He says here,
"Because at the beginning,

00:02:00.923 --> 00:02:04.825
it marks you as a
bodhisattva". It marks you.

00:02:04.825 --> 00:02:08.512
It is what marks you in the
beginning as a bodhisattva.

00:02:08.512 --> 00:02:11.770
It is like you have a sign
on your head or something.

00:02:11.770 --> 00:02:15.182
If you have this kind of compassion.

00:02:15.182 --> 00:02:19.326
I think it is nice to,

00:02:19.326 --> 00:02:21.440
when you talk about compassion

00:02:21.440 --> 00:02:26.440
in the seven-step cause and
effect bodhichitta training,

00:02:26.600 --> 00:02:29.250
I think it is good if you
talk about compassion.

00:02:29.250 --> 00:02:34.167
You think about pain, shared, shared pain.

00:02:35.240 --> 00:02:38.620
I think compassion means

00:02:38.620 --> 00:02:41.520
that you empathize with other people.

00:02:41.520 --> 00:02:45.615
Compassion always implies

00:02:45.615 --> 00:02:48.370
that you have had some pain yourself.

00:02:48.370 --> 00:02:50.240
Then when you see other people having it,

00:02:50.240 --> 00:02:52.030
you feel compassion.

00:02:52.030 --> 00:02:55.279
So I think compassion
is sort of an experience

00:02:55.279 --> 00:02:58.970
of sharing pain in this world.

00:02:58.970 --> 00:03:02.000
This world is painful for everybody.

00:03:02.000 --> 00:03:03.840
The biggest people to the smallest people

00:03:03.840 --> 00:03:07.160
have the same pain. And
it is a shared experience.

00:03:07.160 --> 00:03:10.074
It is something that
brings us all together.

00:03:10.074 --> 00:03:11.258
It should bring us together.

00:03:11.258 --> 00:03:14.240
I think, we get into pain

00:03:14.240 --> 00:03:17.050
and we get grumpy. Then
we fight with each other.

00:03:17.050 --> 00:03:19.660
But really we are all
experiencing the same pain.

00:03:19.660 --> 00:03:22.720
We are all falling down
in the same airplane.

00:03:22.720 --> 00:03:25.762
I think pain should bring us together.

00:03:25.762 --> 00:03:29.770
We should think, "I am
having pain today in my foot

00:03:29.770 --> 00:03:33.090
and everyone else around me
is having some kind of pain."

00:03:33.090 --> 00:03:37.800
It should make us softer
to each other, I think.

00:03:37.800 --> 00:03:42.453
So, he says at the beginning,
this kind of compassion,

00:03:43.330 --> 00:03:46.990
it marks you as a bodhisattva.

00:03:46.990 --> 00:03:51.967
It is the, ultimately, this
kind of empathy where you think,

00:03:51.967 --> 00:03:55.078
"I am having the same
pain as you are having,"

00:03:55.078 --> 00:03:57.810
is what is going to take us to
the vision of a bodhisattva.

00:03:57.810 --> 00:04:01.000
Eventually, that kind of thinking

00:04:01.000 --> 00:04:04.620
that everybody around me has
some kind of pain going on,

00:04:04.620 --> 00:04:05.893
that kind of thinking

00:04:05.893 --> 00:04:08.280
is what is going to
make you a bodhisattva.

00:04:08.280 --> 00:04:10.610
So, it is not very hard.

00:04:10.610 --> 00:04:14.090
It is not very difficult to acknowledge

00:04:14.090 --> 00:04:16.680
that everyone around us

00:04:16.680 --> 00:04:19.670
is having the same kind of
problems that we are having.

00:04:19.670 --> 00:04:21.810
Today was my foot, or somebody else.

00:04:21.810 --> 00:04:24.682
It is not a big logical leap

00:04:24.682 --> 00:04:28.200
to understand that everyone
has something going on.

00:04:28.200 --> 00:04:33.200
Then that is a very powerful
seed, says Chandrakirti,

00:04:34.230 --> 00:04:37.904
that is a powerful seed for bodhichitta.

00:04:37.904 --> 00:04:40.362
BAR DU in the next paragraph.

00:04:40.362 --> 00:04:42.036
RGYAL SRAS KYI SPYOD PAR
MI ZHUM PA'I GO CHA'I

00:04:42.036 --> 00:04:45.594
BRTZON 'GRUS SKYED PAS
CHU LUD LTAR GAL CHE BA

00:04:47.910 --> 00:04:49.120
So, that is at the beginning,

00:04:49.120 --> 00:04:53.690
and now in the interim, during our work

00:04:53.690 --> 00:04:58.690
on the spiritual path, this
compassion is like water.

00:04:58.860 --> 00:05:00.430
Or he says here LUD

00:05:00.430 --> 00:05:02.060
which means fertilizer,

00:05:02.060 --> 00:05:04.883
like water or fertilizer on the tree.

00:05:05.830 --> 00:05:08.680
Why? Because if you have

00:05:08.680 --> 00:05:13.090
that kind of shared suffering,

00:05:13.090 --> 00:05:15.006
feeling we are in this together,

00:05:15.006 --> 00:05:16.590
if you have this kind of attitude,

00:05:16.590 --> 00:05:20.793
that we are all in this pain together,

00:05:21.770 --> 00:05:23.860
that is a kind of GO CHA.

00:05:23.860 --> 00:05:26.037
What is GO CHA, you guys remember?

00:05:26.037 --> 00:05:28.787
Varma? Varman?

00:05:31.850 --> 00:05:36.850
Armor, knight's armor, the
steel coat that you put on.

00:05:37.440 --> 00:05:40.923
So, after you get on the spiritual path,

00:05:41.900 --> 00:05:46.490
this awareness that we
are all having problems.

00:05:46.490 --> 00:05:51.490
We are all suffering pretty
equally. It is like armor.

00:05:52.500 --> 00:05:56.282
Armor means for your BRTZON 'GRUS.

00:05:56.282 --> 00:05:59.170
BRTZON 'GRUS means

00:05:59.170 --> 00:06:01.250
when you do your Buddhist practice,

00:06:01.250 --> 00:06:04.190
you do it in a good mood.

00:06:04.190 --> 00:06:06.750
You are not like a grumpy bodhisattva.

00:06:06.750 --> 00:06:11.040
You are like, "Yeah, we
are all having trouble,

00:06:11.040 --> 00:06:14.380
and okay, what the heck?

00:06:14.380 --> 00:06:16.946
Come on, let us do something
good with our lives.

00:06:16.946 --> 00:06:19.570
Let us do something beautiful together."

00:06:19.570 --> 00:06:21.430
So, it is a kind of BRTZON 'GRUS

00:06:21.430 --> 00:06:26.330
that compassion or that
empathy with other people,

00:06:26.330 --> 00:06:29.743
where we are all aware
that we all have problems.

00:06:29.743 --> 00:06:32.810
It is hard to say whose
problems are worse.

00:06:32.810 --> 00:06:34.570
We all have problems.

00:06:34.570 --> 00:06:39.420
And keeping that in mind is like an armor

00:06:39.420 --> 00:06:42.200
or a shield that protects your joy.

00:06:42.200 --> 00:06:44.490
It protects your joy with your practice.

00:06:44.490 --> 00:06:46.040
Then you do not get too serious.

00:06:46.040 --> 00:06:48.385
You do not get grumpy.

00:06:48.385 --> 00:06:49.933
You are like, "Okay, I can do this."

00:06:49.933 --> 00:06:54.933
And it protects you from
breakdowns, practice breakdowns.

00:06:55.230 --> 00:06:57.610
By the way, if you never
had a practice breakdown,

00:06:57.610 --> 00:07:00.830
it is because you are not practicing.

00:07:00.830 --> 00:07:05.553
So, Grandpa has a practice
breakdown every two days.

00:07:06.790 --> 00:07:09.020
If you do not have a practice breakdown,

00:07:09.020 --> 00:07:11.780
I think you are not a
human being, or something.

00:07:11.780 --> 00:07:15.530
We all mess up. We all
have practice breakdown.

00:07:15.530 --> 00:07:17.229
But if you remember,

00:07:17.229 --> 00:07:20.670
that we are all suffering
pretty much the same,

00:07:20.670 --> 00:07:24.860
then your practice
breakdowns will be shorter

00:07:24.860 --> 00:07:26.900
and you will come back
to your practice quicker.

00:07:26.900 --> 00:07:31.270
But by the way, if you have
a breakdown in your practice,

00:07:31.270 --> 00:07:33.850
you get depressed, you
do something terrible

00:07:33.850 --> 00:07:36.210
that you thought you would not do again,

00:07:36.210 --> 00:07:38.127
then just get back up%

00:07:38.127 --> 00:07:40.602
and think, "Everyone is messed up.

00:07:40.602 --> 00:07:42.460
We are all messed up equally.

00:07:42.460 --> 00:07:45.230
Come on, let us get back on the horse

00:07:45.230 --> 00:07:46.990
and let us keep going."

00:07:46.990 --> 00:07:49.988
All right, so, that is
beginning and interim.

00:07:49.988 --> 00:07:52.128
THA MAR means, in the next paragraph,

00:07:52.128 --> 00:07:53.528
THA MAR SANGS RGYAS THOB NAS KYANG

00:07:53.528 --> 00:07:55.145
It is very interesting

00:07:55.145 --> 00:07:58.880
that even after you achieve enlightenment,

00:07:58.880 --> 00:08:00.780
you reach Buddhahood,

00:08:00.780 --> 00:08:02.380
so yeah, you should not need

00:08:02.380 --> 00:08:05.850
the steps to get
bodhichitta anymore, right?

00:08:05.850 --> 00:08:08.020
Like, if you reached Buddhahood,

00:08:09.130 --> 00:08:13.390
maybe you outgrew six of the seven steps.

00:08:13.390 --> 00:08:14.700
It makes sense.

00:08:14.700 --> 00:08:16.940
I already reached the bodhisattva.

00:08:16.940 --> 00:08:19.150
So I do not need the
first six steps anymore.

00:08:19.150 --> 00:08:21.600
And Chandrakirti says,
"Uh-uh, no, no, no, no, no.

00:08:21.600 --> 00:08:23.725
Do not think like that."

00:08:23.725 --> 00:08:27.400
Buddhas enjoy peach fruits.

00:08:27.400 --> 00:08:29.650
Buddhas enjoy their enlightenment.

00:08:29.650 --> 00:08:33.470
Buddhas enjoy the feeling
of shared empathy also.

00:08:33.470 --> 00:08:36.360
They do not give it up
after they become a Buddha.

00:08:36.360 --> 00:08:39.377
When you become a full bodhisattva,

00:08:39.377 --> 00:08:41.440
when you finally reach bodhichitta,

00:08:41.440 --> 00:08:45.120
which is that vision of a bodhisattva,

00:08:45.120 --> 00:08:47.090
when you finally reach that,

00:08:47.090 --> 00:08:50.550
it is not like you outgrow compassion.

00:08:50.550 --> 00:08:55.510
Compassion then becomes
some kind of delicious fruit

00:08:55.510 --> 00:08:59.226
that you can keep eating forever,

00:08:59.226 --> 00:09:01.990
for billions of lives, forever.

00:09:01.990 --> 00:09:04.460
So it is not like you outgrow it.

00:09:04.460 --> 00:09:08.340
You need it as a seed for
your bodhisattva practice.

00:09:08.340 --> 00:09:12.610
You need it to protect your joy
while you are a bodhisattva.

00:09:12.610 --> 00:09:15.790
And then you are going
to sit and chew on it

00:09:15.790 --> 00:09:16.960
after you become a Buddha,

00:09:16.960 --> 00:09:20.570
and just enjoy the
feeling of shared empathy.

00:09:20.570 --> 00:09:23.975
All right, we are going to
go onto the next topic here.

00:09:23.975 --> 00:09:25.483
BYANG CHUB KYI SEMS

00:09:25.483 --> 00:09:29.960
SHUGS DRAG LOD KYANG 'DI'I RJES SU 'GRO

00:09:29.960 --> 00:09:33.860
This feeling of shared suffering

00:09:33.860 --> 00:09:37.430
is going to determine the DRAG LOD

00:09:37.430 --> 00:09:40.150
in the middle of the next line. DRAG LOD.

00:09:40.150 --> 00:09:43.150
That feeling of shared suffering

00:09:43.150 --> 00:09:47.140
is what is going to decide the DRAG LOD

00:09:47.140 --> 00:09:48.094
of your bodhichitta.

00:09:48.094 --> 00:09:50.561
DRAG LOD means

00:09:50.561 --> 00:09:53.760
if you are playing a guitar

00:09:53.760 --> 00:09:56.900
you stretch the string very tight,

00:09:56.900 --> 00:09:58.540
that is called DRAG.

00:09:58.540 --> 00:10:00.400
And then you loosen the string,

00:10:00.400 --> 00:10:01.690
it is called LOD, okay?

00:10:01.690 --> 00:10:02.800
So DRAG LOD means

00:10:02.800 --> 00:10:06.290
how tight is the string on your guitar.

00:10:06.290 --> 00:10:08.813
It is called DRAG LOD.

00:10:08.813 --> 00:10:12.226
What does it mean with bodhichitta?

00:10:12.226 --> 00:10:17.207
Whether your vision of the
future of jumping across planets

00:10:19.040 --> 00:10:23.570
is strong or kind of floppy,

00:10:23.570 --> 00:10:26.020
is determined by your compassion.

00:10:26.020 --> 00:10:28.660
So, the compassion is the hand

00:10:28.660 --> 00:10:30.720
which is tightening the string.

00:10:30.720 --> 00:10:35.230
And if your shared feeling of suffering

00:10:35.230 --> 00:10:36.717
is strong,

00:10:36.717 --> 00:10:41.717
then your bodhichitta is tight
and makes a beautiful sound.

00:10:42.530 --> 00:10:45.850
If your compassion is lazy, and

00:10:45.850 --> 00:10:49.050
you do not think about how we
are all suffering together,

00:10:49.050 --> 00:10:50.891
then it is going to be

00:10:50.891 --> 00:10:53.616
your bodhichitta will
also be kind of sloppy

00:10:53.616 --> 00:10:58.616
and loose. Boing, boing.

00:10:59.045 --> 00:11:02.642
BYANG SEMS RNAMS KYANG SA
LAM BGROD TSUL MYUR BUL

00:11:02.642 --> 00:11:05.430
So MYUR BUL is a parallel

00:11:05.430 --> 00:11:06.754
to DRAG LOD.

00:11:06.754 --> 00:11:10.312
DRAG LOD means how tight is the string?

00:11:10.312 --> 00:11:13.180
MYUR BUL means how fast is the progress?

00:11:13.180 --> 00:11:14.650
How fast does the car go?

00:11:14.650 --> 00:11:18.690
Here we have a picture of a car.

00:11:18.690 --> 00:11:20.910
I do not know, when I was a teenager,

00:11:20.910 --> 00:11:24.860
this was heaven to get a car.

00:11:24.860 --> 00:11:29.780
The day I met Veronica, I was
under a race car, fixing it.

00:11:33.081 --> 00:11:36.590
I saw her feet first.

00:11:36.590 --> 00:11:39.248
And so for, I don´t know,

00:11:39.248 --> 00:11:43.230
for an Arizona boy, a
fast car is like heaven.

00:11:43.230 --> 00:11:46.910
How fast is your bodhichitta?

00:11:46.910 --> 00:11:49.977
How fast are you going to travel the path?

00:11:49.977 --> 00:11:51.380
SA LAM

00:11:51.380 --> 00:11:54.270
How fast are you going to
go through the five paths?

00:11:54.270 --> 00:11:55.490
How fast are you going to go

00:11:55.490 --> 00:11:57.204
through the ten bodhisattva levels?

00:11:57.204 --> 00:12:02.204
It all depends on how
strong is your feeling

00:12:02.261 --> 00:12:05.445
that we are all going
down in the same airplane.

00:12:05.445 --> 00:12:08.688
We are all in the same boat.

00:12:08.688 --> 00:12:11.196
SNA TSOGS 'BYUNG BA'I RTZA
BA SNYING RJE SHUGS CHE CHUNG

00:12:11.196 --> 00:12:12.029
LAS BYUNG

00:12:12.029 --> 00:12:14.910
He has three pairs of words here.

00:12:14.910 --> 00:12:19.251
He has: DRAG LOD - MYUR BUL - CHE CHUNG

00:12:19.251 --> 00:12:22.084
DRAG LOD - MYUR BUL - CHE CHUNG

00:12:23.064 --> 00:12:26.970
The tightness of your compassion

00:12:26.970 --> 00:12:30.545
determines your bodhichitta.

00:12:30.545 --> 00:12:35.000
The speed that you are going to go,

00:12:35.000 --> 00:12:38.112
MYUR BUL, fast or slow,

00:12:38.112 --> 00:12:39.900
is determined by your compassion

00:12:39.900 --> 00:12:44.900
and SHUGS CHE CHUNG
means big or small power.

00:12:45.308 --> 00:12:46.560
Vega

00:12:46.560 --> 00:12:51.560
SHUGS to your shared feeling of pain,

00:12:53.320 --> 00:12:55.510
sharing pain with others.

00:12:55.510 --> 00:13:00.500
All right, that is how it
makes your car go faster.

00:13:00.500 --> 00:13:02.075
All right, next paragraph.

00:13:02.075 --> 00:13:04.225
BYANG CHUB SEMS DPA' SNGAGS LA ZHUGS NAS

00:13:04.225 --> 00:13:06.616
MYUR LAM 'TSOL ZHING,

00:13:06.616 --> 00:13:08.350
Then he says a very interesting thing,

00:13:08.350 --> 00:13:11.560
he is like, "Look, everybody knows

00:13:11.560 --> 00:13:14.370
that if you really want to help people,

00:13:14.370 --> 00:13:17.020
you should practice the Diamond Way,

00:13:17.020 --> 00:13:18.600
the secret teachings, okay?

00:13:18.600 --> 00:13:21.268
If you really want to help people,

00:13:21.268 --> 00:13:24.543
then you should practice the Diamond Way,

00:13:24.543 --> 00:13:25.900
or the secret teachings.

00:13:25.900 --> 00:13:29.108
Why? Because it is faster.

00:13:29.108 --> 00:13:31.890
You can reach enlightenment

00:13:31.890 --> 00:13:36.170
in one lifetime instead of
a few billion lifetimes,

00:13:36.170 --> 00:13:40.010
if you practice Diamond Way.

00:13:40.010 --> 00:13:42.630
Then he challenges us, very interesting.

00:13:42.630 --> 00:13:45.700
Pabongka says, "Hey, do
you want to take a guess?

00:13:45.700 --> 00:13:50.260
Why it is faster?

00:13:50.260 --> 00:13:53.790
Do you want to guess why it is faster."

00:13:53.790 --> 00:13:55.157
And then you are supposed to say,

00:13:55.157 --> 00:14:00.157
"I know from what you just said,"

00:14:00.605 --> 00:14:02.560
Tantra must be faster

00:14:02.560 --> 00:14:05.400
because you have more compassion.

00:14:05.400 --> 00:14:09.260
Maybe that is why secret
teachings work faster.

00:14:09.260 --> 00:14:13.273
Maybe if you dial up your
compassion to much higher level,

00:14:15.560 --> 00:14:18.227
that is what makes Diamond Way faster.

00:14:18.227 --> 00:14:20.738
BGROD PA SHIN TU MYUR BA
YANG SNYING RJE'I STOBS

00:14:20.738 --> 00:14:24.350
SNYING RJE'I STOBS it is
the power of compassion

00:14:24.350 --> 00:14:26.910
that makes Tantra faster.

00:14:26.910 --> 00:14:31.910
